        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "995b031d-eee0-5e8d-ae3b-7ec1c9c327fe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nic Nolan, Lachlan Murdoch\n- Organizations: 5AA, NOVA Entertainment, Illyra\n- Places: Chiswick, London, England, Adelaide, Australia\n- Roles: broadcast journalist, communications consultant, Programme Director\n- Topics: commercial talkback radio, radio ratings\n\nFacts:\n- Nic Nolan was born on 1 May 1958 in Chiswick, London, England.\n- Nic Nolan is an Australian broadcast journalist and communications consultant who works with private enterprise and with State and Local Government in Australia.\n- From 2004 to 2008, Nic Nolan was Programme Director of Adelaide's number one Newstalk radio station 5AA.\n- During 2004 to 2008, 5AA achieved 32 consecutive breakfast number ones and 11 consecutive 10+ number one ratings victories.\n- 5AA, identified as FIVEaa, is Adelaide's only commercial talkback radio station.\n- 5AA is 50% owned by NOVA Entertainment and Lachlan Murdoch's company Illyra.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
